\end{itemize} 
Motivated by \eqref{favoured-numbers}, the inequality \eqref{Frostman-nonspecial-scales} is proved in two cases. If $\tilde{\ell}_r \notin \mathscr{D}_m$ for some $r \in \{0, 1, \ldots, j-1\}$, then \eqref{favoured-numbers} says that all the basic intervals $\mathtt I(\mathbf i_m) \subseteq I_{\ell}(j)$ belong to $\mathscr{J} \setminus \mathscr{J}^{\ast}$ and therefore receive the same mass $(1 - \varepsilon_m) \mathtt s_m^{-(\mathtt b_m - \mathtt a_m)}$. Applying this along with the already established ball condition \eqref{ball-condition} for $\mathtt I(\mathbf i_{m-1})$, \eqref{Nm-lower-bound}, and \eqref{ambm-take-2}, we arrive at
